node_modules/
dist/

# ─── Course material — deliberately never committed ────────────────────────────
# `sources/` is a clone of the course's own repositories, and everything the
# pipeline writes under `public/` is derived from it: the lesson pages, the
# figures, and verbatim interpreter source files. That material belongs to the
# BGU course staff, not to this repo — it is fetched and generated locally by
# `npm run setup && npm run pipeline:parse`. See README → "What is not in here".
sources/
public/content/
public/resources/

# Translation worksheets are scratch and are regenerated from the pipeline, but the
# two authoring guides are real documentation — the README points at them, so they
# must survive a fresh clone.
work/*
!work/GUIDE.md
!work/GUIDE-CODE.md

# Generated reports
verification-report.md

# TypeScript incremental build cache
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
